<title>NETHERLANDS: Dutch cen banker sees stability pact uncertainty.</title>
<headline>Dutch cen banker sees stability pact uncertainty.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-06-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Incoming Dutch central bank head Arnout Wellink said on Wednesday it was uncertain whether next week's European summit would agree on the EU's budgetary Stability Pact, although he believed it would soon be endorsed.</p>
<p>Wellink said it had been expected important decisions about economic and monetary union (EMU), including the stability pact would be taken at the summit. &quot;As things stand now, however, due to political and domestic reasons, it is uncertain whether agreement could be reached at the summit in Amsterdam,&quot; he said, adding, however, he did not think it was impossible.</p>
</text>
